  "content_en": "3. Unintentional insertion: \"...This can't go on like this, you must persuade me!\" On an autumn afternoon, in the east room of the second courtyard in the southeast corner of the Ningping Marquis Mansion, Mrs. Jiang was sitting on the large Kang by the window in the east room, which was covered with Yun Mang makeup and striped quilts, looking at the woman opposite with a worried face. \"Sister, you think I don't want to, but you don't understand your eldest brother's temper. You originally thought that you would be cheap if you competed with the younger members of the Wang family, but now you are being robbed of them. On the surface, you are fine, but in fact, you are already mad at heart. If this person is full of anger all day long, how can... how can he not be sick? \"Li, sister, tell me... if your eldest brother really can't afford to be ill at this juncture, and Brother Xing is not here, what should I, a woman, do in such a big family...\" This woman is Yan, the wife of Jiang Zhen, the eldest brother of the Jiang family. But at this moment, Yan's fair and smooth face was full of sorrow, and she was complaining sadly. By the end of the sentence, Danfeng's eyes were full of tears and her voice was choked. \"Sister-in-law, please stop being like this. Brother has always been in good health and nothing serious will happen...\" Seeing her like this, Mrs. Jiang couldn't help but feel heartbroken and anxious, and she also shed tears. But she couldn't care less about herself, and quickly comforted Yan while taking the handkerchief from her sleeve and handing it over. \"Hey, I hope so!\" Mrs. Yan took the handkerchief, wiped it on her face, and sighed. The sister-in-law and sister-in-law looked at each other in silence for a while, then Mr. Jiang asked again, \"When will Brother Xing come back?\" \"Um... I guess it will be next spring. The mountains in Dongsheng Prefecture have been snowed and the food stalls have been closed. Fortunately, Brother Xing planned it. \"Good morning, a batch of goods has been sold out and exchanged for banknotes, but if he is not enlightened, he will not be able to come back in time.\" Speaking of her son, the worry on Mrs. Yan's face could not help but fade, and there was a hint of tenderness and relief in her eyes. \"Brother Xing is really promising. When he was older, he went to make money from the Tatars.\" After hearing what his sister-in-law said, a sincere smile appeared on Mrs. Jiang's face. \"What's the future? You're a big man, but you don't like to study. How can you compare to your Brother Shui? Every time my husband mentions it, he is full of praise. The fourth young master of Ningping Marquis Mansion is knowledgeable and hard-working. I will definitely bring you back a scholar in the spring examination next year.\" After hearing this, Mrs. Yan covered her sleeves and said with a smile. \"I'm looking forward to it...\" Although Mrs. Jiang tried her best to be reserved, she still couldn't hold back the smile on her lips. The son is undoubtedly the best and dearest to the mother. Speaking of the son, both of their faces were filled with joy, and the depression in the room was instantly diluted. \"Madam, Miss Ninth is here...\" At this moment, Zhou's mother's voice came from outside the door. Both people in the room were startled. Jiang frowned, while Yan's face darkened. \"Let her come in!\" After a moment of silence, Mrs. Jiang spoke, and then looked at Mrs. Yan, \"This child is not insignificant.\" Mrs. Yan said nothing, just curled her lips and smiled. In a short time, the vermilion-sprinkled door curtain was lifted, and Zhou's mother led a thin figure into the inner room, bypassing the pair of red sandalwood carvings with auspicious details and depicting golden landscape figures called Duobaoge. Jiang's eyes fell on that figure - wearing a double-snail bun that is common for little girls, with fair skin, and although her eyebrows have not faded from childishness, they are soft and delicate, making people look very comfortable. Especially when her eyes fell on Sister Wenjiu's lotus-pink little eight-treasure gauze jacket with hanging threads, her eyes softened even more. This was the one she had cut for Sister Ten when it was just cold. Because it was too big and didn't fit, she decided to give it to her, and then cut a new one for her own daughter... \"Mother! Auntie!\" Looking at the two people sitting on the kang, Sister Wenjiu naturally did not dare to be rude and quickly bowed to salute them. Mrs. Jiang asked Mrs. Zhou to bring a brocade table for her to sit on, while Mrs. Yan had a few lively words with her. Of course, Sister Wenjiu didn't think she was popular because of this. In the two years since she came to this other world and lived in this big house, what she had learned most was to observe people's emotions. She had already noticed the lukewarm look on Jiang's face and the lack of interest in Yan's eyes. Especially when she stood under the veranda and saw Zhou's mother standing at the door, she had already realized that she might not have come at the right time. Mother Zhou was the third lady's companion and confidant, but she was sent to guard the door. She thought that the conversation between the third lady and her uncle and grandma must be extraordinary. In fact, if Zhou's mother hadn't seen her at that time, she would have already made the return trip... \"Mom, I'll ask my uncle to take care of me today.\"Thanks to the candles my mother sent me, my daughter made a little gadget and now she brings it to her mother and aunt to relieve their boredom! \"She didn't pull at the ones that were there, let alone pretend to be mysterious, but directly took out the half of the colorful candle that Qingtao had just wrapped in a brocade handkerchief. The bright and lovely shape of the colorful candle made the eyes of several people in the room light up instantly, especially Yan's pair of languid eyes. \"Mother Zhou, can you please help light this candle? \"Sister Wenjiu looked at Zhou's mother inquiringly. \"Mom, aunt, look at this candle wick... My daughter just tried it. There is no need to cut the candle flowers with these three threads...\" The candle was lit and burning slowly. In the fragrance that spread in the room, Sister Wenjiu explained to the two of them in detail. \"Sister Jiu, not only are you good at this candle, but the idea of ​​these three cotton wicks is even more amazing. Sister-in-law, don't you think so? \"Yes, yes, you said that there are so many masters in our Jiang Family Wax Workshop, why don't we have such a good idea...\" \"Actually, it's nothing...\" Facing the probing gazes of the two people, Sister Wen Jiu turned her eyes away, feeling quite embarrassed. He said, \"I made this candle originally just because I wanted to fill in the dowry box for my third sister, but I didn't expect that... I had no intention of doing it...\" Mrs. Jiang didn't say anything. Mrs. Yan was surprised when she heard the words. When she was about to ask more questions, she saw Jiang's hand The tea cup was placed on the table gently. Yan smiled knowingly and stopped continuing the topic. Seeing this, Sister Wenjiu felt relieved, but at the same time, she also secretly reminded herself to be cautious in the future and remember to hide her clumsiness. None of the women in the inner house are vegetarians...--------Digression----Happy Christmas Eve, my dears, I'm sorry, it's a very busy Christmas Eve, so it's even later! Remember to eat apples, haha...",
